\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.17}{\ignorespaces Reverse obstacle maneuvering with and without the deterministic safety gate, learned policy against pure pursuit on the same hard-layout-dominated pool. Without a gate the learned attempt-versus-abort decision already keeps the learned policy far safer than pure pursuit, which cannot decline a layout. Adding the gate drives the crash rate to near zero for both and leaves their completion comparable. Reference seed. Commit-success is completions over completions plus crashes.\relax }}{57}{table.caption.61}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:safety_gate}{{4.17}{57}{Reverse obstacle maneuvering with and without the deterministic safety gate, learned policy against pure pursuit on the same hard-layout-dominated pool. Without a gate the learned attempt-versus-abort decision already keeps the learned policy far safer than pure pursuit, which cannot decline a layout. Adding the gate drives the crash rate to near zero for both and leaves their completion comparable. Reference seed. Commit-success is completions over completions plus crashes.\relax }{table.caption.61}{}}
